                <pb facs="0791" n="781" xml:id="pg781"/>

                <head>Appendix H to HD–76</head>
                <p rendition="#center"><hi rendition="#italic">Note Delivered by Baron von Lersner,
                        October 23, 1919</hi></p>
                <p>For several weeks Flensburg has been suffering from gross excesses committed by
                    strikers and members of the seamen’s league. Crews who wish to work are
                    threatened; provisioning is jeopardized. On the 16th instant the Hotel de Ville
                    was taken by assault and impossible demands made on the magistrates.
                    Consequently, we were obliged to comply with the urgent request of the
                    authorities and of the citizens of Flensburg to take measures for military
                    protection.</p>
            </div>
